* n3_rect1_inv120: single-phase fully controlled bridge, 230 V, alpha=120 deg, load Linv
* Behavioural thyristor: series diode + gate-controlled conductance (50 mohm on) that latches while I > IH (5 mA).
* Gate pulses rise in 20 us: faster edges stall the WASM solver at the commutations.
.subckt SCR A K G
Vs A x 0
D1 x y DSCR
Gsw y K cur = V(y,K)*(1e-6 + 20*V(ctl))
Bset c0 0 V = 1-(1-0.5*(1+tanh(20*(V(G,K)-0.5))))*(1-0.5*(1+tanh(2000*(I(Vs)-5m))))
Rc c0 ctl 1k
Cc ctl 0 10n
.model DSCR D(IS=1e-12 N=1.5 RS=5m CJO=100p)
* keeps the inner node defined while both parts are off
Ry y K 1e7
* RC snubber across the device (100 ohm + 22 nF), as in practice (section 10.6)
Rsn A sn 100
Csn sn K 22n
.ends

VS a0 b SIN(0 325.2691 50)
LSRC a0 a 50u IC=-10.0000
RB b 0 1m
XT1 a p g1 SCR
XT2 n b g2 SCR
XT3 b p g3 SCR
XT4 n a g4 SCR
VG1 g1 p PULSE(0 5 0.006666666666666666 20u 20u 1m 20m)
VG2 g2 b PULSE(0 5 0.006666666666666666 20u 20u 1m 20m)
VG3 g3 p PULSE(0 5 0.016666666666666666 20u 20u 1m 20m)
VG4 g4 a PULSE(0 5 0.016666666666666666 20u 20u 1m 20m)
VSENSE p p1 0
LL p1 m 2 IC=10
RL m e 1
VE e n -113.5364
.options method=gear reltol=1e-3 vntol=1e-4 abstol=1e-9 itl4=100
.tran 5u 100m 0 5u uic
.save v(p) v(n) v(a) v(b) i(VSENSE) i(VS)
.end
